# Baseline security headers for the STATIC side of the site.
#
# worker/index.js sets the same set on the responses it generates itself,
# but those two paths are genuinely separate: wrangler.jsonc only routes
# /share/* through the Worker (run_worker_first), so every other request is
# answered straight from the asset layer and never reaches that code. This
# file is what covers those. Verified in production: before it existed,
# /share/* carried the headers and / did not.
#
# Not set here, on purpose:
#   - a general Content-Security-Policy. The site loads Google Fonts, the
#     Spotify iframe API, self-hosted tesseract wasm and inline styles; a
#     script-src/style-src policy needs each of those proven first, and a
#     wrong one breaks the game quietly. frame-ancestors is the one
#     directive safe in isolation — it governs who may embed US, not what
#     the page may load.
#   - Strict-Transport-Security. It is a commitment covering every present
#     and future subdomain of the apex and cannot be withdrawn inside its
#     own max-age. That is a deliberate decision, not a line in a header
#     pass.
#
# Permissions-Policy names only features this codebase never calls (checked:
# no getUserMedia, no geolocation, no payment request). Clipboard and Web
# Share are deliberately unlisted — they default to same-origin and the
# share/copy flows depend on them.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), magnetometer=(), gyroscope=(), accelerometer=()
